BOM fix:
```ts
function encodeBodyLosslessly(body: Buffer) {
  try {
    // ignoreBOM: 保留开头 BOM，保证文本 -> 字节可无损还原（默认行为会丢弃 BOM）
    const text = new TextDecoder('utf-8', { fatal: true, ignoreBOM: true }).decode(body);
    return { encoding: 'utf-8' as const, content: text };
  } catch {
    return { encoding: 'base64' as const, content: body.toString('base64') };
  }
}
```

Wait — does TextDecoder ignoreBOM:true + fatal:true work together? Yes, independent options.

Hmm, one more consideration: with ignoreBOM: true, a body of exactly "EF BB BF" decodes to "\uFEFF" — valid. Re-encode → EF BB BF. Lossless ✓.

But also there's another losslessness concern: TextDecoder fatal mode with valid UTF-8 — decoding then re-encoding is always identity for valid UTF-8? Yes, UTF-8 decode/encode is a bijection on valid sequences (canonical — well, valid UTF-8 decoded to string then re-encoded gives the same bytes, since decoders reject overlong forms with fatal... actually overlong forms are invalid UTF-8, fatal rejects → base64. So yes, lossless).

